          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "8. Approximately what percentage of Family C’s expenses were on housing?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.157,
            0.881,
            0.196
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Was it as straightforward to answer these questions as the earlier questions?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.196,
            0.881,
            0.234
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Is there a visualisation that makes it simpler to answer such questions?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.234,
            0.882,
            0.294
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Look at the following visualisation of the same data. Try to understand how the chart is organised and answer the three questions above."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "chart",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.122,
            0.312,
            0.876,
            0.478
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "chart_body",
              "index": 6,
              "bbox": [
                0.122,
                0.312,
                0.876,
                0.478
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_12_chart_6.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "chart_caption",
              "index": 7,
              "bbox": [
                0.235,
                0.486,
                0.763,
                0.505
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 10.2: A Stacked Bar Chart of the data in Table 10.2"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.52,
            0.883,
            0.693
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Such a graph/chart is called a "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "stacked bar or column chart",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". Bars within a cluster are joined one after the other in a particular order. "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Stacked bar charts are used when we want to compare the totals but also want to keep track of the components that make up the totals.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Here, the total length of a full stacked (combined) bar represents the total expenditure of a family in that month. Also, the length of a smaller bar and the full stacked bar can be compared to get an estimate of what fraction or percentage the smaller bar makes up of the full stacked bar."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.693,
            0.881,
            0.731
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Now, use the stacked bar chart to answer the Questions 1–5 shown earlier."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.73,
            0.849,
            0.75
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Is it possible? Is it easy? If not, what made it harder than before?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.75,
            0.884,
            0.866
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Except for the first small bar, the rest of the stacked small bars do not begin from 0. This makes it a little harder to estimate the quantity corresponding to a bar. Also, bars across clusters need not have a common base or a starting point. So, comparing bars within clusters and across clusters may be harder. However, seeing the totals of all the clusters is easier."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
